<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gobind Sagar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1963</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gobind Sagar is a reservoir on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a> in the Bilaspur and Una districts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, formed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhakra-dam">Bhakra Dam</a>, completed in 1963. Named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guru-gobind-singh">Guru Gobind Singh</a>, it stretches for about 90 km and submerged the old town of Bilaspur and many villages. It is used for fishing and water sports.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gobind-sagar.jpg" alt="Gobind Sagar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ambuj Mishra · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gobind_Sagar_Lake_Ambuj.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
